    <heading level="1">Extensions</heading>
    <paragraph>Recall from Rotation of Axes that equations of conics with an $$xy$$ term have rotated graphs. For the following exercises, express each equation in polar form with $$r$$ as a function of $$\theta.$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="56" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$xy = 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="57" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x^{2} + xy + y^{2} = 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$r=\pm 2 1+sin\theta cos\theta r=\pm 2 1+sin\theta cos\theta$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="58" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$2x^{2} + 4xy + 2y^{2} = 9$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="59" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$16x^{2} + 24xy + 9y^{2} = 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$r=\pm 2 4cos\theta +3sin\theta r=\pm 2 4cos\theta +3sin\theta$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="60" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
